# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Lakshmi Shenoy et al. (2024). Collinear-spin machine learned interatomic potential for Fe7Cr2Ni alloy.
#   Physical Review Materials. doi:10.1103/physrevmaterials.8.033804  arXiv:2309.08689v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2309.08689v2 (sha256 220416807634163d...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 448 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/shenoy2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the VASP (PBE, collinear AFM spins) training database
# DB1-8 of Fe7Cr2Ni bulk and monovacancy supercells with short-range order
# from KKR-CPA effective-medium Monte Carlo, strains, relaxation
# trajectories and AIMD snapshots (about 160,000 atomic environments),
# and three GAPs (2-body plus SOAP; 6 A cutoffs): standard GAP, Spin GAP
# with Fe spin-augmented descriptors and compressed (spin) GAP variants.
# Errors are given only as bounds or approximate improvements (gaps);
# elastic constants, vacancy energies and magnetic behaviour are
# properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
