###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Errors are stated only as bounds or relative changes: energy training and test errors within 2 and 6 meV/atom, force errors as low as 200 meV/A (low temperature) and 400 meV/A (high temperature) for GAP; Spin GAP lowers typical energy errors by about 1 meV/atom and force errors by about 50 meV/A. Per-model values are in figures (Figs. 3, A2).
# - The spin-augmented and compressed descriptors are encoded as settings of GAP. Lattice parameters, elastic constants (Table III), vacancy formation energies and magnetic properties are properties.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/shenoy2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
